<title>THAILAND: Bovis gets Thai supermarket contract.</title>
<headline>Bovis gets Thai supermarket contract.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bovis (Thailand) Ltd, a unit of Bovis Construction Group, said on Thursday that it received a contract worth 1.2 billion baht ($48 million) to refurbish and manage the construction of supermarkets in Thailand.</p>
<p>&quot;We will develop and refurbish existing TOPS Supermarkets nationwide, as well as construct 20 new outlets, giving them all a new modern image,&quot; said Kim McLure, country manager of Bovis (Thailand), in a statement.</p>
<p>The project is scheduled to start in early 1997 and end in 2000.</p>
<p>TOPS Supermarkets is a joint venture between Thailand's Central Department Store and the Netherlands-based TOPS Supermarkets (Royal Ahold).</p>
<p>Bovis Construction Group is a wholly owned subsidiary of the London-based P&amp;O Group.</p>
<p>($1 = 25 baht)</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
</text>
